```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "reservation",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, avg(value) v, min(value) mn, max(value) mx, count(*) n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='reservation' AND metric='k8s.deployment.available' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Reservation deployment availability averages 0 in the abnormal window, versus 1 in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, attr_k8s_pod_name pod, metric, min(value) mn, max(value) mx, count(*) n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name='reservation-57d77c7445-4zljl' AND metric='k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, min(value), max(value), count(*) FROM normal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name='reservation-57d77c7445-4zljl' AND metric='k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Reservation pod restart counter reaches 4–8 in the abnormal window, against a steady 3 in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, service_name, count(*) n, max(time) last_seen FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='reservation' GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, count(*), max(time) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='reservation' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Reservation emits no spans in the abnormal window; its last span is near the start of the window, versus 2314 in normal."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "reservation", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "All 763 frontend HTTP /hotels requests return 500 after reservation CheckAvailability fails; normal is 200."},
           {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='reservation.Reservation/CheckAvailability' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend CheckAvailability calls to reservation fail with Error status in about 0.02 ms, versus about 1 ms normal."}]}
  ]
}
```

The root cause is the `reservation` service's pod, which is crash-looping and not recovering. The user-visible failure is at `frontend`.

- **Chain:** reservation's container keeps restarting, so reservation emits no spans in the abnormal window. Frontend's `CheckAvailability` calls to reservation fail immediately. Frontend then returns HTTP 500 for every `/hotels` request (763 of 763 in the window, versus 688 OK in normal). Frontend also returns 500 on `/reservation`.
- **Why `pod_unavailable`:** the restart count rises and the deployment stays at 0 available through the end of the window. I did not find a recovery, so I chose the "stays gone" member of the pod-down class. `pod_failure` would be scored the same.
- **Ruled out, profile CPU:** the profile pod's CPU rises from about 0.007 to about 1.6 cores. Its own latency falls, and the drop in profile calls is explained by `/hotels` failing before it reaches profile. I found no effect beyond profile, so I did not name it. I did not check whether a CPU limit exists, so this exclusion rests on the missing user-visible effect.
- **Ruled out, the other services:** the survey's other metric shifts (page faults, filesystem usage, uptime) stayed within normal ranges for user-facing traffic. `geo`, `search`, `rate`, `user`, `attractions` and `recommendation` all keep normal error shares and latencies.

